<section class="section" id="published">
    <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Published</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="entries">
        <li class="entry">
            <div class="entry-meta"><span>Jun 2025 – Jul 2026</span><span>ICTAI 2026</span></div>
            <div class="entry-body">
                <h3 class="entry-title"><a href="/research/llm-ocr/">Improving LLM-Based OCR Through Document Segmentation and Semantic Prompting</a></h3>
                <p class="entry-context">Co-author · accepted to ICTAI 2026</p>
                <p>
                    A two-stage pipeline: a layout model segments the page, and a vision-language model reads it
                    with that structure as context. I owned the first stage, building the benchmark that puts
                    Detectron2, MinerU, and LayoutParser on common ground. The models segment pages at
                    different granularities, so naive scoring punished detail rather than error; normalizing
                    the bounding boxes cut benchmarking error by 40%.
                </p>
                <p class="entry-stack">Python, PyTorch, TensorFlow, Detectron2, MinerU, LayoutParser</p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>

